{"text": "The incident reporting and investigation process is a critical component of the health and safety management system, designed to ensure that all workplace incidents, including near misses, are promptly reported, thoroughly investigated, and effectively addressed to prevent recurrence. When an incident occurs, the first step is for the employee involved or a witness to report the incident immediately to their supervisor using the standardized incident report form. The supervisor is responsible for ensuring that the incident is documented accurately and submitted to the health and safety department within 24 hours. Upon receiving the report, the health and safety officer initiates an investigation to determine the root cause of the incident. This involves gathering evidence, interviewing witnesses, and reviewing relevant documentation. The findings of the investigation are compiled into a detailed report, which includes recommendations for corrective actions to mitigate future risks. The report is then reviewed by the health and safety committee, which is responsible for approving the proposed corrective actions and ensuring their implementation. Once the corrective actions are in place, the health and safety officer monitors their effectiveness and provides feedback to the committee. This process not only helps in maintaining a safe working environment but also fosters a culture of continuous improvement in health and safety practices.", "name": "Incident Reporting and Investigation Process", "id": 0, "category": "", "tokens": [{"text": "The", "indexInDocument": 0, "posTag": "DT", "sentenceIndex": 0}, {"text": "incident", "indexInDocument": 1, "posTag": "NN", "sentenceIndex": 0}, {"text": "reporting", "indexInDocument": 2, "posTag": "NN", "sentenceIndex": 0}, {"text": "and", "indexInDocument": 3, "posTag": "CC", "sentenceIndex": 0}, {"text": "investigation", "indexInDocument": 4, "posTag": "NN", "sentenceIndex": 0}, {"text": "process", "indexInDocument": 5,